-# SVG Texture
-
-## What it is
-- **An SVG Texture is an ordinary `UTexture2D`** made by importing a `.svg`, so every texture picker (a Brush's Image), `Set Brush From Texture`, Image Size on drop and thumbnails work as for any image. The SVG and its settings ride on it as Asset User Data: **`UWidgetSVGTextureData`** (`UAssetUserData`, `NameTBD/Widgets/WidgetSVGTexture.h`, editor-only: `IsEditorOnly` strips it when cooking, so a game has only the texture).
-- **Earlier designs, and why not:**
-  - v1, a `UTexture2D` subclass: `UTexture2D` is `MinimalAPI` and most of its virtuals aren't exported, so a plugin subclass fails to link (LNK2001 on `Serialize`, `PostLoad`, `CreateResource`...).
-  - fix1, a `UObject` owning a texture behind `ISlateTextureAtlasInterface`: the Brush's Image picker didn't list it.
-  - Only exported or virtual calls are made on textures: member settings, `Source.Init` / `UseHashAsGuid`, `PreEditChange` / `PostEditChange` (all linked in fix1), and `IInterface_AssetUserData` (`AddAssetUserData`, `GetAssetUserDataOfClass`) through the interface.
-- **Fidelity:** drawn (editor only) into the texture's source pixels at **Resolution Scale** (default 4) x the SVG's own size (width/height, else viewBox), the longest side held to **Max Resolution** (default 2048). `ApplyTextureSettings` sets the texture up on import: `TC_EditorIcon` (uncompressed RGBA), sRGB, `TEXTUREGROUP_UI`, Never Stream, **mips (`TMGS_SimpleAverage`)**. So it is sharp at and below Resolution Scale x its size and filters cleanly when drawn smaller. Image Size on drop is the texture's size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size).
-- **Colours (the "black SVG" fix):**
-  - **Colors** (`TArray<FWidgetSVGColor>`, `EditFixedSize`) lists every colour the SVG uses (fills, strokes, gradient stops; first-use order; opacity left out), with **Draw As** next to each. Draw As alpha multiplies the SVG's own opacity.
-  - **Draw In White (Tint With Brush)** (`bDrawInWhite`, default off) draws every colour white keeping opacity, so the Brush Tint / Color and Opacity colours it. A shape with no fill is black in SVG: that is the black entry.
-  - Both are edited in an **SVG** category at the top of the texture's Details (the Texture Editor), shown only on textures that carry the data: `FWidgetSVGTextureDetails`, a class layout registered on `Texture2D`, adds the data object's properties as external object rows, so edits go to the data object.
-- **Redraw:** editing Resolution Scale, Max Resolution, Draw In White or Colors redraws from `SVGSource` (the file's text, kept on the data) into its outer texture. `PreEditChange(nullptr)` waits for a running build, then `Source.Init`, then `PostEditChange`. Not while a picker/spin box is dragged (`Interactive` changes are skipped). Undo redraws from the restored settings. Reimport reads the file again, keeping each still-present colour's Draw As.
-
-## Pieces
-- **Rasterizer:** nanosvg, vendored header-only in `Source/ThirdParty/nanosvg` (upstream commit and licence in its README), on `NameTBD`'s private include path.
-  - Compiled only in `WidgetSVGTexture.cpp` under `WITH_EDITOR`, as C++ inside `namespace NameTBDNanoSVG` (`NANOSVG_CPLUSPLUS` / `NANOSVGRAST_CPLUSPLUS`; the C headers it uses are included first, outside the namespace), so it never clashes with the engine's own copy.
-  - Output is straight (not premultiplied) RGBA with edge colours spread into clear pixels; swapped to BGRA for `Source.Init(..., TSF_BGRA8)` + `UseHashAsGuid`.
-- **Recolouring** edits the parsed `NSVGshape` paints (`0xAABBGGRR`) before rasterizing; `RasterizeSVG` also refreshes `Colors` (only assigned when it differs).
-- **Editor** (`NameTBDEditor/Private/WidgetSVGTextureFactory.*`):
-  - `UWidgetSVGTextureFactory`: text factory for `svg`, priority `DefaultImportPriority + 10`. It makes the `UTexture2D`, adds the data, and draws. It is also the `FReimportHandler`, for textures carrying the data, at a priority above the engine's texture reimporter.
-  - `FWidgetSVGTextureDetails`: registered and unregistered in `NameTBDEditor.cpp`.
-
-## Checked outside the engine
-- nanosvg in the namespace compiles with g++ and links beside a plain C copy (no duplicate symbols); an SVG path with no fill parses as `0xFF000000` and draws white after recolouring; gradient stops are reached and recoloured.
-
-## Still open
-- **SVG features nanosvg lacks:** `<text>`, filters, masks, clip paths, `<use>`/symbols, most CSS (`<style>` beyond simple cases), images. Such parts are dropped. A file that relies on them needs flattening (e.g. text to paths) before import.
-- **Image Size on drop** is the texture size (Resolution Scale x the SVG size), not the SVG size: a plain Texture 2D can't report another size. Set Image Size by hand, or Resolution Scale 1 for an exact match (and less sharpness).
-- Sharp beyond Resolution Scale x the size needs a higher scale (more memory) - there is no runtime re-draw at the widget's size.
-
-## Unverified (no engine here)
-- That it compiles against 5.7: `UTexture::AssetImportData` being reachable, `IInterface_AssetUserData` on `UTexture`, `AddExternalObjectProperty`, and `UAssetUserData` being subclassable from a plugin.
-- That a class layout on `Texture2D` is applied alongside the engine's `Texture` one (details customizations apply per class in the hierarchy), and that nothing else in the engine registers `Texture2D`.
-- That non-power-of-two sizes get mips in 5.7 (if not, such SVG Textures have none and are less clean when drawn smaller).
-- That the factory wins `.svg` over Interchange / Epic's SVG Importer when those are on.
